### The fix: dependency injection

Instead of creating the Claude client inside the function you want to test, pass it in as a parameter. Then tests can pass a fake one.

```js
// Hard to test — client is baked in
async function summarize(text) {
  const client = new Anthropic();
  const res = await client.messages.create({ ... });
  return res.content[0].text;
}

// Testable — client is a parameter
async function summarize(text, client) {
  const res = await client.messages.create({ ... });
  return res.content[0].text;
}

// In production code:
await summarize(text, new Anthropic());

// In a test:
const mockClient = {
  messages: { create: async () => ({ content: [{ text: 'Mocked summary.' }] }) }
};
await summarize(text, mockClient);
```

